Z||000003||Raydar||02-09-2001||03:01 PM||||Kev,<P>I don't know that I would go that high on an 87 coupe. Depends on what it's worth to you, though.<BR>I'm pretty sure that it'll be a good car. Sounds like it was well cared for. <BR>IMHO, you could probably find a d@mn nice Formula or pre-88 GT for that kind of money.<P>------------------<BR>Raydar - aka Steve<P>88 T-top Formula<BR>88 soon-to-be-V6 coupe||||reg||1
Z||000004||Haze_Performance||02-09-2001||03:14 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by KEV:<BR><B>I'M LOOKING AT A 87 BASE COUPE WITH 26,000 MILES ON IT, IT HAS A/C,STEREO,A/T,C/C. IT WAS OWNED BY A LITTLE OLD LADY THAT BOUGHT IT WHEN SHE WAS 69 IT HAD THE OIL CHANGED EVERY 1,000 MILES AND A BRAKE JOB AT 24,000 NOT BAD. IT'S FOR SALE FOR $4500 DO YOU THINK IT'S TO MUCH?  yes i did see it, it's black the paint is perfect.<P>[This message has been edited by KEV (edited 02-09-2001).]</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P><BR>Well... last year I bought a '85 Sport Coupe w/38,000 miles. I paid $2500 & it was loaded. (A/C, Auto, WS6 Sus, PW ect...) I for one like the look of a coupe. Offer around $3500 for it and see where it goes. Alot of people down the coupes because theres GT's & Forumlas to compare to. I for one feel that if you buy any car that cheap & its relible, then go for it..<P>There to many GT huggers out there...<B>THE COUPES WILL RISE AGAIN!!!!!!!! BAND TOGETHER MY BROTHERS!!!!!</B><P>Ohhh  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/redface.gif"> sorry....... I like GT's too ...<P><BR>Carl  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> <P><BR><P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/ttttttt.gif">  <BR><A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/WS6_Fiero/photo.html" TARGET=_blank><BR>WS6 Fieros "Members Photo Page"</A>||||reg||10
Z||000005||ChadMan||02-09-2001||04:15 PM||||Even with the low mileage, I'd say $4500 is too much.  There's a guy in Venice, FL selling a Formula with a nice red repaint and a little over 50K miles for $4495 right now.<P>Realistically, it is probably worth around $3K, but if you've fallen in love with it, it wouldn't hurt to offer $3500.  The DIS Dukes tend to be pretty reliable -- mine certainly has been (except for the stumbling problem).||||reg||13
